<BaseLayout title="About" description="Meet Zeeshan Haider: a multidisciplinary designer with an IT background and international project experience.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="hero-columns"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / ABOUT</span><h1 class="page-title">A little more <span class="soft">human.</span></h1><p class="page-lead">I’m Zeeshan, a multidisciplinary designer based in Lahore. I work across visual communication and user interfaces, and I’m learning more about the development side of the web.</p></div><div class="aside-note">Professional experience is only part of the story. This space is deliberately more personal.</div></div></div></section>
<section class="inner-section"><div class="container split"><div class="profile-portrait"><span class="monogram">ZH.</span><span class="pic-tag">Personal photograph to be added</span></div><div><span class="eyebrow">HELLO AGAIN</span><h2 class="small-title">Design is where my creative and technical interests meet.</h2><div class="body-copy"><p>My work has taken me across graphic design, brand identities, social media campaigns, websites, applications and admin-panel interfaces. I like that each format asks for a different kind of thinking — from expressive communication to careful information design.</p><p>I studied Business &amp; Information Technology at the University of the Punjab, and that background gives me an interest in how products work beyond their visuals.</p><p>Now I'm beginning to explore front-end development. I'm not presenting myself as an experienced developer; I'm interested in learning through practical work and sharing that progress.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/resume/">Explore my experience ↗</a></div></div></section>
<section class="inner-section muted-bg"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">HOW I APPROACH WORK</span><h2 class="section-title">A mix of craft and curiosity.</h2></div><p class="section-description">Three threads that connect the different things I work on.</p></div><div class="triple-grid"><div class="info-card"><span class="micro">01 / VISUAL</span><h3>Clarity in communication</h3><p>Designing creatives and brand systems that communicate clearly across formats and audiences.</p></div><div class="info-card"><span class="micro">02 / INTERFACE</span><h3>Thinking in systems</h3><p>Structuring screens, interactions, and visual hierarchy so products feel more coherent.</p></div><div class="info-card"><span class="micro">03 / GROWTH</span><h3>Learning by building</h3><p>Developing front-end fundamentals as a natural extension of a design-led practice.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="inner-section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">BEYOND THE SCREEN</span><h2 class="small-title">More than job titles.</h2><div class="body-copy"><p>I'm leaving room here for the things that make the site feel personally mine — interests, routines, inspirations, what I enjoy outside client work, and a little of my personality.</p><p>Those details will come from me directly rather than being invented to fill the page.</p></div><span class="tag">Personal details coming later</span></div><div class="quote-panel">Thoughtful design starts with paying attention — to people, purpose and the little details.</div></div></section>
